description:
memory.rs:198-214 — recompute_calendars_with_events:

  fn recompute_calendars_with_events(&mut self, account_id: &str) {
      let events = self
          .objects
          .get(&("CalendarEvent", account_id.to_owned()))
          .cloned()         // <-- clones the entire HashMap<Id, serde_json::Value>
          .unwrap_or_default();

      let mut set: HashSet<Id> = HashSet::new();
      for value in events.values() {
          if let Some(map) = value.get("calendarIds").and_then(|v| v.as_object()) {
              for k in map.keys() {
                  set.insert(Id::from(k.as_str()));
              }
          }
      }
      self.aux_mut(account_id).calendars_with_events = set;
  }

The .cloned() at line 202 is exactly the 'clone-to-escape-borrow-checker' pattern that AGENTS.md flags. The clone exists because we cannot hold an immutable borrow of self.objects while also taking a mutable borrow via self.aux_mut(). The fix is to restructure as a two-phase build:

  fn recompute_calendars_with_events(&mut self, account_id: &str) {
      let set: HashSet<Id> = self
          .objects
          .get(&("CalendarEvent", account_id.to_owned()))
          .into_iter()
          .flat_map(|m| m.values())
          .filter_map(|v| v.get("calendarIds").and_then(|c| c.as_object()))
          .flat_map(|map| map.keys().map(|k| Id::from(k.as_str())))
          .collect();
      self.aux_mut(account_id).calendars_with_events = set;
  }

This drops the immutable borrow at the end of the chain expression, then takes the mutable borrow. No cloning of the event map. CalendarEvent payloads carry full JSON bodies (recurrence rules, participant lists, alerts, attachments) — cloning them just to read keys from one nested map is real, observable work.

The call site (memory.rs:701, 759, 789) runs this on every CalendarEvent create/update/destroy, so this is per-mutation overhead in the reference impl that contributors will read as 'this is how a MemoryBackend re-indexes derived state'.
